NAME
       reset - put the terminal back into a sane state

SYNOPSIS
       reset

DESCRIPTION
       After a program crashes or you print a binary file with cat, the
       terminal can be left with strange characters, no echo or broken line
       endings. reset sets the terminal's modes back to the defaults and
       clears the screen. If you cannot see what you type, type reset
       blindly and press Enter (or Ctrl+J).

EXAMPLES
           reset

SEE ALSO
       clear(1), stty(1)
